  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Leidos reported federal contract obligations of $1.9B for FY2026 to date. Leidos recorded 2,507 awards with an average award size of $772K. Leidos obligations fell 36.3% year over year. Leidos received the largest portion of obligations from the Department of Defense at $1.5B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $234M and the Department of Transportation at $131M. Leidos work is concentrated in Computer Systems Design Services at $612M and Computer Facilities Management Services at $530M, with additional activity in Electronic Computer Manufacturing at $283M and Electronic and Precision Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $227M. Fiscal-year obligations peaked at $3B in FY24 and FY25, and FY26 to date matches FY21 at $1.9B. The data reflect partial current-year totals, and award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Leidos’ federal business trended year over year?",
        "body": "Leidos obligations fell 36.3% year over year. Leidos reported $1.9B in obligations for FY26 to date, down from $3B in FY25 and FY24. Leidos obligations in earlier years were $2.6B in FY23, $2.7B in FY22, and $1.9B in FY21."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are Leidos’ largest customers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $1.5B to Leidos in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $234M and the Department of Transportation obligated $131M, followed by the General Services Administration at $75.1M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $35.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
